  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "GSearch: add custom URIResolver for basic auth and SSL, proposed by Ross Wayland:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "\"",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "I'm investigating using fedoragsearch to index additional(other than DC) metadata datastreams that are in the foxml object. The additional metadata datastreams are stored as Managed-content datastreams so I was planning to get at this content using the xslt document() function to retrieve the contents of these datastreams. e.g.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "document('",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://ross.lib.virginia.edu:8080/fedora/get/uva-lib:100/META')"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://ross.lib.virginia.edu:8080/fedora/get/uva-lib:100/META')",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This technique works just fine provided api-a is open. When api-a is using basic auth and/or SSL then the underlying URL looks like:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "document('",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://ross.lib.virginia.edu:8443/fedora/get/uva-lib:100/META')"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://ross.lib.virginia.edu:8443/fedora/get/uva-lib:100/META')",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This method does not work since apparently the default URIResolver of the xslt engine does not know how to deal with basic auth and/or SSL. ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "\"",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "It seems that the right approach is to write a custom URIResolver and let it be configurable, which URIResolver to use with the Transformer.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
